            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnosis of autosomal monogenic hypercholesterolemia using lymphocytes as test material (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>285-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The significance of genetic factors contributing to the complex etiology of coronary heart disease is discussed using lipoprotein metabolism as an example. A radiochemical screening method was developed fro precise biochemical diagnosis of autosomal monogenic hypercholesterolemia. In this method lymphocytes are used as test material.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
